# This snippet diverts the protected paths to the "tps" service, which presents
# a Turnstile challenge designed to prevent bot traffic.
#
# See docs/install/bot-protection.md for usage and bot protection details.

# Protected endpoints:
#
# - /data/* is for raw files - humans can browse and scrape data, but they have
#   to get through the challenge first (making automated harvesting tough, but
#   they can deal with that in a browser, then copy the token or something;
#   there's no easy way to protect this path otherwise, and SEO / AI bots
#   generally don't belong here)
# - /search/* should never be crawled by any bots, period
# - /issues/* is the calendar view, and while it's not expensive, it's a waste
#   of resources for bots to "click" through every link just to get data
#   already in our sitemap
# - /lccn/<lccn>/issues/first_pages/* is the per-title issue browser, which is
#   arguably great for bots to discover issues, but very expensive (see gh
#   #643), and bots should be given a sitemap anyway
#
# All paths live in a single path_regexp, with each protected prefix being one
# alternative in the group. Matchers listed inside a named matcher are ANDed
# together, so OR-ing paths has to happen within one matcher - and keeping it
# to one matcher means shared rules (like a client_ip exemption) only ever
# need to be written once.
@protected {
  path_regexp ^/(data/|search/|issues/|lccn/\w+/issues/first_pages/)
  # not client_ip blah blah
}

handle @protected {
  reverse_proxy tps:8080
}
